From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mpl: exact fixed-outline packing check

checkPacking() decides whether rectangles fit in a fixed outline without
overlap, with OR-tools CP-SAT, which OpenROAD already links: rigid blocks
with one or more shapes, soft blocks whose height is floor(area / width)
as SoftMacro computes it, and fixed blocks. The answer is kFits with a
placement, kDoesNotFit with a cause (a block too wide or too tall, the
area, or the arrangement), or kUndecided when the deterministic budget
runs out; it does not depend on machine load or thread scheduling.

Cheap bounds and constructions settle most problems first: a block that
fits nowhere, the area, blocks wider than half the outline that must
stack, identical blocks that must fit as a grid, and a shelf packing. The
rest go to CP-SAT on a ladder of grids, coarse first: rounding blocks up
gives placements legal at full resolution, rounding them down gives
proofs that nothing fits. Nothing calls it yet.

Not upstreamed; retires at the //:bump onto an OpenROAD that has it.

---
